stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Idle
    Idle --> Selecting: start region / supervisor owns slurp
    Idle --> Starting: start monitor
    Selecting --> Starting: valid selection
    Selecting --> Idle: Escape
    Selecting --> Cancelling: stop terminates owned slurp
    Cancelling --> Idle: selection reaped
    Cancelling --> Saving: recorder reaped
    Starting --> Recording: recorder started
    Starting --> Idle: startup fails or stop requested
    Recording --> Paused: pause signals owned recorder
    Paused --> Recording: resume
    Recording --> Cancelling: stop
    Recording --> Saving: recorder exits
    Paused --> Cancelling: stop
    Paused --> Saving: recorder exits
    Saving --> Idle: wait for recorder, move capture, release lock
    note right of Selecting
        No timeout changes user-paced selection to Idle.
        One supervisor owns children and publishes state.
        QML watches state; it does not infer it from process names.
    end note
